WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.648 line:85%
After developing our emulator, we built a
Node-RED dashboard to track the machine's
status in real time,

2
00:00:07.648 --> 00:00:11.400 line:85%
with the option to change the interface
theme and language.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.773 line:85%
We can then choose the control source,

4
00:00:14.773 --> 00:00:17.220 line:85%
either our emulator or the PC directly.

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.397 line:85%
For this demonstration,

6
00:00:19.397 --> 00:00:23.700 line:85%
we use the emulator and start the machine's
normal operation.

7
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.692 line:85%
The synoptic view animates the cooling
circuit,

8
00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:28.980 line:85%
and no fault is detected for now.

9
00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:33.360 line:85%
Now to the first failure, characterized by a
pressure drop.

10
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.759 line:85%
We can simulate this anomaly,

11
00:00:35.759 --> 00:00:41.130 line:85%
set the playback speed and choose the
starting position in the data replayed by
the emulator.

12
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:47.900 line:85%
This lets us watch the parameters evolve and
follow the machine's behavior during this
degradation.

13
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.760 line:85%
The gauge shows the predicted failure risk,

14
00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:56.700 line:85%
and the curve compares the estimated
remaining useful life with the actual one,
until the failure is detected.

15
00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:00.930 line:85%
We now move to the second scenario, high
pressure.

16
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:01.937 line:85%
At first,

17
00:01:01.937 --> 00:01:06.590 line:85%
the parameters stay in a normal state and
the failure risk stays low.

18
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.890 line:85%
Then the random forest model detects a
degradation in operation.

19
00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.993 line:85%
From that detection,

20
00:01:12.993 --> 00:01:18.070 line:85%
the LSTM model estimates the time remaining
before a possible machine failure.

21
00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.418 line:85%
As you can see, our chatbot answers our
questions:

22
00:01:22.418 --> 00:01:26.650 line:85%
it confirms the fault, gives the remaining
useful life and says what to do.

23
00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.400 line:85%
Finally, we simulate a leak in the cooling
circuit.

24
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.614 line:85%
As in the previous scenarios, we watch the
parameters evolve,

25
00:01:35.614 --> 00:01:42.680 line:85%
the random forest model detecting the
degradation, then the LSTM model estimating
the time to failure.

26
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:49.900 line:85%
The dashboard thus gives the operator time
to plan maintenance before the failure
occurs.
